{
 "manufacturer": "Siemens",
 "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
 "model": "SITRANS F M MAG 6000 with USM II Modbus RTU module",
 "model_slug": "sitrans-f-m-mag-6000-modbus",
 "short_model": "MAG 6000",
 "aliases": [
  "MAG 6000",
  "MAG 6000 I",
  "SITRANS FM MAG 6000"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Sensor (flow transmitter)",
 "applies_to": "SITRANS F M MAG 6000 / MAG 6000 I electromagnetic flow transmitters fitted with the USM II Modbus RTU RS-485 add-on module (operating instructions 03/2021).",
 "summary": "The MAG 6000 electromagnetic flow transmitter gets a Modbus RTU slave by fitting the USM II RS-485 add-on module. Data is held in holding registers and coils only. This map covers volume flow and totalizers (float and double), driver and identity registers, basic, totalizer, output, input, sensor and display settings, system status and the totalizer/batch/zero-adjust coils.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 19200,
  "parity": "Even",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "Every row prints both the Modbus register (4:0xxxx / 0:0xxxx, 1-based) and the Modbus address (0-based) sent on the wire; this map uses the address column. The manual's own example reads absolute massflow 4:03001 with query address 0x0BB8 (3000)."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "SITRANS F Modbus RTU RS 485 (USM II) communication module, Operating Instructions",
  "doc_number": "A5E00753974-AB",
  "revision_date": "2021-03",
  "url": "https://cache.industry.siemens.com/dl/files/906/44880906/att_70364/v1/A5E00753974-ABen_USMII_MODBUS_AOM_OI_en-US.pdf",
  "pages": "process data p. 37-38; driver/application settings pp. 38-40; MAG 6000 settings tables A-8, A-10, A-12, A-14, A-16, A-18, A-20, A-22, A-25 pp. 40-58; status p. 57; coils pp. 64-66; float definition pp. 71-72; factory settings p. 21"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Word order: the manual states the module is big-endian, most significant byte first, and its float table and example frame (4:03001 read as 40 C3 52 93 = 6.10383 kg/s) put the high word in register N. Floats, doubles and double words are therefore listed as ABCD.",
  "'Byte' values sit in the low byte of one register and are listed as UINT16 (0-255).",
  "Units of the process values and totalizers follow the unit registers (2904-2917, ID tables in Appendix B.1/B.2). The 'point' registers set the number of decimals (0-6) shown on the display.",
  "Adding 10000 to the address of a writable register returns its minimum allowed value, adding 20000 returns its maximum (these mirror registers are not listed).",
  "Values printed as (1/100%) are fractions where 1.0 = 100 % (the manual's example: 0.02 = 2 %).",
  "Left out: capability bits (603, 3-byte array) and the 54-byte error pending / error log lists (2702, 2729); their record layout is in Appendix B.4.",
  "Error numbers are listed in the SITRANS F M / F C transmitter operating instructions, not in this manual.",
  "MAG 6000 has no mass, density or temperature values; 3000 and 3004-3012 are MASS 6000 only.",
  "Volume flow (3002) and totalizers are in the customer units set at 2906, 2912 and 2914 (defaults m3/s and m3); Q max and other settings are always in m3/s / m3."
 ],
